===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*strew-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|construccioun}}, {{m|enm|construction}}, from {{der|en|fro|construction}}, from {{der|en|la|cōnstructiō}}, from {{m|la|cōnstruō|cōnstruere}}.

Morphologically {{suffix|en|construct|-ion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/kənˈstɹʌkʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-construction.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ʌkʃən|s=3}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{senseid|en|process}} The [[process]] of [[constructing]].
#: {{ux|en|'''Construction''' is underway on the new bridge.}}
#* {{quote-web|en|title=RAP Benefits for Pavement Owners|url=https://www.asphaltpavement.org/uploads/documents/Sustainability/NAPA_RAP_Benefits_for_Pavement_Owners_1121.pdf|page=1|work=National Asphalt Pavement Association|passage=89.2 million tons of RAP are used annually in new asphalt pavement '''construction''' in the United States.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250321011807/https://www.asphaltpavement.org/uploads/documents/Sustainability/NAPA_RAP_Benefits_for_Pavement_Owners_1121.pdf}}
# {{senseid|en|result}} Anything that has been constructed.
#: {{ux|en|The engineer marvelled at his '''construction'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|trade}} The [[trade]] of [[building]] [[structures]].
#: {{ux|en|He had worked in '''construction''' all his life.}}
# {{senseid|en|model}} A building, [[model]] or some other [[structure]].
#: {{ux|en|The office was a '''construction''' of steel and glass.}}
# {{senseid|en|arts}} {{lb|en|arts}} A (usually non-representational) structure, such as a [[collage]] etc.
#: {{ux|en|"'''Construction''' in string and clockwork" took first prize.}}
# {{senseid|en|manner}} The [[manner]] in which something is built.
#: {{ux|en|A thing of simple '''construction'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913|author=[[w:Robert Barr (writer)|Robert Barr]]
|title=Lord Stranleigh Abroad
|chapter=4|url=http://openlibrary.org/works/OL1796924W
|passage=Nothing could be more business-like than the '''construction''' of the stout dams, and nothing more gently rural than the limpid lakes, with the grand old forest trees marshalled round their margins like a veteran army that had marched down to drink, only to be stricken motionless at the water’s edge.}}
# {{senseid|en|grammar}} {{lb|en|grammar}} A [[group]] of [[word]]s arranged to form a [[meaningful]] [[phrase]].
# {{senseid|en|construing}} The act or result of [[construing]] the meaning of something.
#: {{ux|en|American conservatives tend to favor strict '''construction''' of the Constitution.}}
# {{senseid|en|interpretation}} The [[meaning]] or [[interpretation]] of a text, action etc.; the way something is viewed by an observer or onlooker.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1992|author=Hilary Mantel|title=A Place of Greater Safety|publisher=Harper Perennial|year_published=2007|page=95
|passage=He had considered sending Lucille away to stay with relations. But then people might have put the worst '''construction''' on it – might believe she had done something she shouldn't have.}}
# {{senseid|en|geometry}} {{lb|en|geometry}} A geometric figure of arcs and line segments that is drawable with a [[straightedge]] and [[compass]].

